Z||000000||kornholio||08-06-99||12:01 PM||||Hi,<br>I have an automatic 86 Fiero SE.  When I shift into drive from park, neutral or reverse, it takes about 2 seconds to kick in. Does anyone know what the problem is?  I know it's not the transmission fluid because I just had it changed.  This is an annoying problem as sometimes I forget to wait for it to kick in and I step on the gas right away. This causes the wheels to spin like crazy. I've been told that if I continue to spin the wheels like that, I will mess up the transmission.  Thanks.
Z||000001||theogre||08-06-99||12:30 PM||||if the filter was changed, and not put in right, it could be slow to pressurize because it's sucking air or partly blocked.<p>you may also have stirred up some dirt when the work was done that has now lodged in something.
